RFC 006: Weather Integration & OpenWeatherMap Bridge
1. System Architecture
RFC 006 defines the asynchronous weather bridge connecting physical real-world weather metrics to in-game environmental state variables via the OpenWeatherMap API [cite: OurVillage].
2. Real-World to In-Game Parameter Mapping
OpenWeather Metric
In-Game Condition
Mechanical Impact
 
Precipitation > 2.0 mm/h
RAIN / STORM
Crop growth tick rate x1.5; outdoor resting efficiency -50%; increases tavern traffic [cite: OurVillage].
Temperature < 0° C
FREEZING / SNOW
Increases firewood consumption rate x2; outdoor resting without shelter causes energy loss [cite: OurVillage].
Clear / Low Wind
SUNNY / CLEAR
Standard crop growth; normal outdoor resting; high market trade volume [cite: OurVillage].

3. Server Weather Tick Schema
The server broadcasts weather updates inside master tick payloads on world/global/time [cite: OurVillage]:
{
  "tick": 8420,
  "in_game_time": "14:00",
  "season": "AUTUMN",
  "weather": {
    "condition": "HEAVY_RAIN",
    "temp_c": 11.2,
    "effects": {
      "crop_growth_multiplier": 1.5,
      "outdoor_rest_penalty": 0.5,
      "firewood_consumption": 1.2
    }
  }
}



